;; manifest/murakumo-accounts.edn — which repository spends under which
;; murakumo credits account.
;;
;; ## Why this is a workspace fact and not a repo's own
;;
;; `scripts/itonami-receipts-export.cljs` folds the murakumo run ledger to give
;; each repo its measured cost. It joins on the spend account, and the ledger
;; keys spending by the JWT `sub` of whoever called `/infer/spend` -- a subject
;; that is issued out of band. Measured twice on 2026-08-31, from the spender
;; side as well as the repo side: nothing in the tree says which repo holds
;; which subject. The production issuer configuration is not here, and the only
;; occurrence of one of these names beside a `sub` is in a test.
;;
;; So the mapping cannot be derived. It has to be declared by someone who
;; knows, and it belongs here rather than in each repo's `actor.edn` because
;; **the spenders are not all actors**. `dougaka` has no `actor.edn` and should
;; not grow one merely to record a billing fact -- an actor.edn is a claim
;; about governance, and this is a claim about a bill.
;;
;; ## The rule this file exists to keep
;;
;; An account nobody claims here is reported UNATTRIBUTED with its credits, and
;; those credits are folded into nobody's cost. Guessing would be worse than
;; the gap: attributing 1,666 credits to the wrong repo produces a margin
;; number that is precise and false.

{:schema 1

 :accounts
 [{:account "dougaka"
   :repo "orgs/cloud-itonami/dougaka"
   :declared-by "Jun Kawasaki"
   :declared "2026-08-31"
   :note "Owner decision. The repo is registered twice in west -- `dougaka` and
          the older `ai-gftd-dougaka`, both at the same revision -- and the
          short name is the one the naming rules prefer. It runs (a
          wrangler.jsonc at its root) and it is the largest spender in the
          ledger, which is what made it the first buyer worth wiring."}]

 ;; Spending accounts seen in the ledger with no declaration yet. Listed so
 ;; the gap is a name rather than a silence; the exporter reports them from the
 ;; ledger regardless, and this is only the reading list.
 :undeclared
 [{:account "shinshi" :seen "2026-08-31" :credits 40.8}
  {:account "isekai-pages" :seen "2026-08-31" :credits 5}
  {:account "did:key:z6MkCustomer2" :seen "2026-08-31" :credits 50
   :note "A did:key rather than a name -- possibly an external customer rather
          than one of ours, which would mean it never gets a repo."}
  {:account "did:key:z6MkVaOUdZOGhInJXDZWPt7OaijGrBB88tjv" :seen "2026-08-31" :credits 50}]}
